{
  "about": "GENERATED \u2014 do not hand-edit `durations`, `tests`, `source` or `partitions`. Run: pnpm run e2e:partitions:generate --from <results.json> --as <label>. Only `about`, `why` and `measuredFrom` are prose, and `pnpm run e2e:partitions:check` guards the rest.",
  "why": "HARDEN-04 / DEBT-128, corrected by HARDEN-06A (F-03). Playwright --shard divides the suite by test COUNT; these seconds are what each spec file actually COSTS, and the partitions below are balanced on them. Every spec file the gate runs MUST appear in `durations`, `tests` and `source` \u2014 `check` fails while any is sized by the `defaultSpecSeconds` guess, because a guess is not evidence and ten of them are what made partition p05 of run 32321840125 exceed globalTimeout with 33 tests never executed.",
  "measuredFrom": [
    "V2.4 FOLLOW-01, 2026-08-26 \u2014 ONE new spec file, MEASURED LOCALLY, and the partition COUNT raised on the arithmetic rather than the coverage trimmed. `follow-01-week-account.spec.ts` is 43.2 s over 4 tests, measured in the sandbox that produced the change from a green run of the file, with `--as local/v2.4-follow-01`. Every other spec file's duration is untouched; 117 of them still read `ci:32605964327` and two read `local/v2.4-gate-02`. The first CI run that publishes this file's artifact should replace it with `ci:<run id>`.",
    "PARTITION_COUNT moved 12 \u2192 13, and this is the question V2.4-GATE-02 told the next item adding E2E coverage to confront. The arithmetic: with the new file measured in, twelve partitions derive a heaviest of 1007.7 s = 16.80 min against the 16.73 min ceiling `MAX_PARTITION_SECONDS` derives \u2014 and it does not fail by a rounding error, because the MEAN of the ten non-sliced partitions is already 1005.0 s, so no packing of any 43-second file fits and reaching the ceiling would mean deleting about a third of the new coverage. Thirteen derives a heaviest of 918.7 s = 15.31 min, 68% of `globalTimeout` \u2014 the same target every split since HARDEN-04 has been tuned to. The ceiling was NOT raised; that is the one answer HARDEN-04 removed from the table.",
    "The new coverage was sized before the count moved, not instead of moving it: the FOLLOW-01 journey was consolidated from 6 tests over 11 page loads to 4 over 8, asserting the same things \u2014 what was removed is redundant page LOADS (a second navigation to re-open the same account at another width, and a separate visit for the Review's phone tier, both now resizes in place), never an assertion.",
    "The COST of thirteen, stated: ~2.3 min more runner time on setup that buys no coverage, and one job past the pool figure interpolated from run 31445526789 \u2014 which measured EIGHTEEN shards queueing, not thirteen, while run 32333645709 measured twelve starting within ONE SECOND of each other with none queued. If the interpolation is right the failure mode is bounded and already written down in `PARTITION_COUNT`: a queued job costs WALL CLOCK and nothing else, because a job that has not started spends none of its `globalTimeout`.",
    "The BETTER fix, measured and deliberately not taken here. `responsive.spec.ts` is 1471.6 s in one generated matrix file and `--shard` is the only way to divide it, so it takes two EXCLUSIVE partitions of 735.8 s apiece against a 1004 s ceiling \u2014 stranding 536 s, 8.9 minutes, of gate capacity that no partition can use, which is why twelve looked exhausted. Recovering it needs either a redesign of `derivePartitions` (both shards of a sliced group must carry an IDENTICAL spec list, or tests are lost and duplicated) or a near-50/50 split of that file into two real spec files. Both change what every partition holds. Raised as its own PRODUCT_DEBT entry with these numbers so the next pass takes it deliberately.",
    "V2.4-GATE-02, 2026-08-25 \u2014 TWO files re-measured LOCALLY, and the exception is stated rather than hidden. `gate-02-honest-signals.spec.ts` is new (40.4 s, 4 tests) and `dhds-13-commercial-quality.spec.ts` grew by one test (70.3 s -> 80.7 s, 12 -> 13). Both were measured in the sandbox that produced the change, from a green run of each file, with `--as local/v2.4-gate-02`. Calibration, so the numbers can be read honestly: the twelve PRE-EXISTING tests of `dhds-13-commercial-quality.spec.ts` measure ~72 s on this machine against CI's 70.3 s, so it is within ~2% of that runner for this workload and the local figures are not systematically optimistic.",
    "V2.4-GATE-01, 2026-08-23. All 117 spec files are measured, every one of them from THE SAME run, and for the first time from a run that was GREEN \u2014 1911 tests collected, 1911 executed, ZERO failed and zero flaky.",
    "GitHub Actions run 32605964327 (ubuntu-latest, workers: 1) at 42afd5f, the twelve-partition gate on the V2.4-GATE-01 branch. All twelve partitions published an e2e-results-<partition> artifact, green ones included \u2014 which is the mechanism DEBT-157 was raised for, and this is its confirming run.",
    "The two shards of e2e/responsive.spec.ts are added together rather than overwriting one another \u2014 the reports hold different tests of one file.",
    "Refresh it the same way: download a run's e2e-results-* artifacts and run pnpm run e2e:partitions:generate --from <each results.json> --as ci:<run id>. pnpm run e2e:partitions:check fails if any spec file on disk is left without a duration, a test count or a source."
  ],
